# Sam

An engineering coworker.

This repo is Sam — identity, scope, capabilities, and runtime. Read `identity.md` to understand who Sam is. Read the files in `capabilities/` to understand how Sam works with specific tools.

## Running Sam

Prereqs on the host:

- Docker and Docker Compose
- `claude login` completed (Sam uses your CC credentials)
- `.env` filled in (see `.env.example`)

Start:

    docker compose up -d

Stop:

    docker compose down

Logs:

    docker compose logs -f sam

## State

Sam's working state lives in `./data/`:

- `data/journal.md` — Sam's append-only journal
- `data/sam.lock` — single-instance lockfile
- `data/repos/` — repos Sam has cloned to work on

This directory is gitignored. Don't commit it.

## Updating Sam

Sam can propose changes to its own source (anything outside `runtime/`) via PR.
The runtime — the body Sam runs in — is not self-modifiable.

Deploys happen manually:

    git pull
    docker compose up -d --build